  "releaseNotes": "LC045 decides whether an invocation is an element-preserving in-memory view once per operation instead of every time it is asked, and rejects non-view operators before probing the cache. Each callback-bearing answer walked the lambda body, so the repetition dominated the rule's cost: lambda-body walks fall 56% on an inline view, 80% on a chained view and 67% on an alias. Diagnostics are unchanged.",
